+{"seq": 105, "ts": 1792081760.54, "role": "tool", "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"exit_code\": 0, \"result\": \"{\\\"cmd\\\": \\\"grep -o 'MECR Mutations Cause Childhood-Onset Dystonia.\\\\\\\\{0,2400\\\\\\\\}' flat8.txt | head -c 2600\\\", \\\"exit_code\\\": 0, \\\"stdout\\\": \\\"MECR Mutations Cause Childhood-Onset Dystonia and Optic Atrophy, a Mitochondrial \\\\\\\\r       Fatty Acid Synthesis Disorder.\\\\\\\\r PG  - 1229-1244\\\\\\\\r LID - S0002-9297(16)30434-7 [pii]\\\\\\\\r LID - 10.1016/j.ajhg.2016.09.021 [doi]\\\\\\\\r AB  - Mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis (mtFAS) is an evolutionarily conserved pathway \\\\\\\\r       essential for the function of the respiratory chain and several mitochondrial \\\\\\\\r       enzyme complexes. We report here a unique neurometabolic human disorder caused by \\\\\\\\r       defective mtFAS. Seven individuals from five unrelated families presented with \\\\\\\\r       childhood-onset dystonia, optic atrophy, and basal ganglia signal abnormalities \\\\\\\\r       on MRI. All affected individuals were found to harbor recessive mutations in MECR \\\\\\\\r       encoding the mitochondrial trans-2-enoyl-coenzyme A-reductase involved in human \\\\\\\\r       mtFAS. All six mutations are extremely rare in the general population, segregate \\\\\\\\r       with the disease in the families, and are predicted to be deleterious. The \\\\\\\\r       nonsense c.855T&gt;G (p.Tyr285(∗)), c.247_250del (p.Asn83Hisfs(∗)4), and splice site \\\\\\\\r       c.830+2_830+3insT mutations lead to C-terminal truncation variants of MECR. The \\\\\\\\r       missense c.695G&gt;A (p.Gly232Glu), c.854A&gt;G (p.Tyr285Cys), and c.772C&gt;T \\\\\\\\r       (p.Arg258Trp) mutations involve conserved amino acid residues, are located within \\\\\\\\r       the cofactor binding domain, and are predicted by structural analysis to have a \\\\\\\\r       destabilizing effect. Yeast modeling and complementation studies validated the \\\\\\\\r       pathogenicity of