1\r\nOT  - TACO1\r\nOT  - TPK1\r\nOT  - TTC19\r\nOT  - UQCRQ\r\nOT  - Nuclear Gene-Encoded Leigh Syndrome Spectrum\r\nOT  - Overview\r\nEDAT- 2025/05/01 00:00\r\nCRDT- 2025/05/01 00:00\r\nAID - NBK320989 [bookaccession]\r\n\r\nPMID- 40204636\r\nOWN - NLM\r\nSTAT- MEDLINE\r\nDCOM- 20250714\r\nLR  - 20260306\r\nIS  - 1550-6606 (Electronic)\r\nIS  - 0022-1767 (Print)\r\nIS  - 0022-1767 (Linking)\r\nVI  - 214\r\nIP  - 5\r\nDP  - 2025 May 1\r\nTI  - Mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis and MECR regulate CD4+ T cell function and \r\n      oxidative metabolism.\r\nPG  - 958-976\r\nLID - 10.1093/jimmun/vkaf034 [doi]\r\nAB  - Imbalanced effector and regulatory CD4+ T cell subsets drive many inflammatory \r\n      diseases. These T cell subsets rely on distinct metabolic programs, modulation of \r\n      which differentially affects T cell fate and function. Lipid metabolism is \r\n      fundamental yet remains poorly understood across CD4+ T cell subsets. Therefore, \r\n      we performed targeted in vivo CRISPR/Cas9 screens to identify lipid metabolism \r\n      genes and pathways essential for T cell functions. Thes"
