tial \r       diagnosis of nuclear gene-encoded LSS with a focus on genetic conditions; 4.. \r       Provide an evaluation strategy to identify the genetic cause of nuclear \r       gene-encoded LSS in a proband (when possible); 5.. Review management of nuclear \r       gene-encoded LSS with a focus on disorders with targeted therapies; 6.. Inform \r       genetic counseling of family members of an individual with nuclear gene-encoded \r       LSS.\r CI  - Copyright © 1993-2026, University of Washington, Seattle. GeneReviews is a \r       registered trademark of the University of Washington, Seattle. All rights \r       reserved.\r FED - Adam, Margaret P\r ED  - Adam MP\r FED - Bick, Sarah\r ED  - Bick S\r FED - Mirzaa, Ghayda M\r ED  - Mirzaa GM\r FED - Wallace, Stephanie E\r ED  - Wallace SE\r FED - Amemiya, Anne\r ED  - Amemiya A\r FAU - Rahman, Shamima\r AU  - Rahman S\r AD  - Professor of Paediatric Metabolic Medicine, Genetics and Genomic Medicine \r       Programme, UCL Institute of Child Health and Great Ormond Street Hospital, \r       London, United Ownerdom\r FAU - Thorburn, David R\r AU  - Thorburn DR\r AD  - Senior Principal Research Fellow, Murdoch Children&#x27;s Research Institute and \r       Genetic Health Services Victoria, Victoria, Australia\r AD  - Royal Children&#x27;s Hospital, Victoria, Australia\r AD  - Department of Paediatrics, University of Melbourne, Melbourne, Australia\r FAU - Ball, Megan\r AU  - Ball M\r AD  - Royal Children&#x27;s Hospital, Victoria, Australia\r AD  - Department of Paediatrics, University of Melbourne, Melbourne, Australia\r AD  - Metabolic Fellow, PhD Candidate, Murdoch Children&#x27;s Research Institute, Victoria, \r       Australia\r LA  - eng\r PT  - Review\r PT  - Book Chapter\r PL  - Seattle (WA)\r OTO - NLM\r OT  - 3-hydroxyisobutyryl-CoA hydrolase, mitochondrial\r OT  - 4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate dioxygenase-like protein\r OT  - 5-taurinomethyluridine-[tRNA] synthase subunit GTPB3, mitochondrial\r OT  - 5-tauri