++{"seq": 61, "ts": 1792081640.691, "role": "tool", "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"exit_code\": 0, \"result\": \"{\\\"cmd\\\": \\\"grep -o 'ES/GS) in the care of pediatric.\\\\\\\\{0,900\\\\\\\\}' flat.txt | head -c 1100; echo; echo ===; grep -o 'ES/GS has a higher diagnostic.\\\\\\\\{0,600\\\\\\\\}' flat.txt | head -c 800; echo; echo ===; grep -o 'TI  - .\\\\\\\\{0,200\\\\\\\\}' flat.txt | head -6; echo ===; grep -o 'FAU - [A-Za-z ,.-]*' flat.txt | sort -u | head -20\\\", \\\"exit_code\\\": 0, \\\"stdout\\\": \\\"ES/GS) in the care of pediatric patients with one or \\\\\\\\r       more congenital anomalies (CA) with onset prior to age 1 year or developmental \\\\\\\\r       delay (DD) or intellectual disability (ID) with onset prior to age 18 years. \\\\\\\\r       METHODS: The Pediatric Exome/Genome Sequencing Evidence-Based Guideline Work \\\\\\\\r       Group (n = 10) used the Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development and \\\\\\\\r       Evaluation (GRADE) evidence to decision (EtD) framework based on the recent \\\\\\\\r       American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics (ACMG) systematic review, and \\\\\\\\r       an Ontario Health Technology Assessment to develop and present evidence summaries \\\\\\\\r       and health-care recommendations. The document underwent extensive internal and \\\\\\\\r       external peer review, and public comment, before approval by the ACMG Board of \\\\\\\\r       Directors. RESULTS: The literature supports the clinical utility and desirab\\\\n\\\\n===\\\\nES/GS has a higher diagnostic \\\\\\\\r       yield and may be more cost-effective when ordered early in the diagnostic \\\\\\\\r       evaluation. CONCLUSION: We strongly recommend that ES/GS be considered as a \\\\\\\\r       first- or second-tier test for patients with CA/DD/ID.\\\\\\\\r CI  - © 2021. The Author(s), under exclusive licence to the American College of Medical \\\\\\\\r       Genetics and Genomics.\\\\\\\\r FAU - Manickam, Kandamurugu\\\\\\\\r AU  - Manickam K\\\\\\\\r AD  - Division of Genetic and Genomic Medicine, Department of Pediatrics, Nationwide \\\\\\\\r       Children&#x27;s Hospital, Columbus, OH, USA.\\\\\\\\r AD  - The Ohio State University College of Medicine,\\\\n\\\\n===\\\\nTI  - Ophthalmic manifestations of MEPAN syndrome.\\\\\\\\r PG  - 469-474\\\\\\\\r LID - 10.1080/13816810.2022.2135112 [doi]\\\\\\\\r AB  - BACKGROUND: Mitochondrial enoyl CoA reductase protein-associated \\\\\\\\r       neurodegenera\\\\nTI  - A mouse model of MEPAN demonstrates a role for mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis \\\\\\\\r       in iron-sulfur cluster and supercomplex formation.\\\\\\\\r PG  - e2506761122\\\\\\\\r LID - 10.1073/pnas.2506761122 [doi]\\\\\\\\\\\\nTI  - Exome and genome sequencing for pediatric patients with congenital anomalies or \\\\\\\\r       intellectual disability: an evidence-based clinical guideline of the American \\\\\\\\r       College of Medical Genet\\\\n===\\\\nFAU - Beauplan, Maina\\\\nFAU - Biswas, Sawona\\\\nFAU - D\\\\nFAU - Demmer, Laurie A\\\\nFAU - Gospe, Sidney M , III\\\\nFAU - Gupta, Priya R\\\\nFAU - Haltom, Jeffrey A\\\\nFAU - Hisama, Fuki M\\\\nFAU - Janssen, Kevin A\\\\nFAU - Kearney, Hutton M\\\\nFAU - Keller, Kierstin\\\\nFAU - Malinowski, Jennifer\\\\nFAU - Manickam, Kandamurugu\\\\nFAU - Massingham, Lauren J\\\\nFAU - McClain, Monica R\\\\nFAU - Miller, Danny\\\\nFAU - Mitchell, Katherine L\\\\nFAU - Murdock, Deborah G\\\\nFAU - O\\\\nFAU - Wallace, Douglas C\\\\n\\\", \\\"stderr\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"sandbox\\\": \\\"sandbox: docker[busybox] (fs=C:/Users/agent/work/project/test-runs/test7-doctor/t7-20261015-215453-0b70, network=off)\\\"}\", \"truncated\": false, \"total_bytes\": 3201, \"artifact_ref\": null, \"duration_ms\": 0}", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95aa43b47cb54329", "name": "run_command", "step": 24}
