++{"seq": 64, "ts": 1792081646.624, "role": "assistant", "content": "Three abstracts verified: the ACMG ES/GS guideline (PMID 34211152), the MEPAN ophthalmology case series (PMID 36262091), and the PNAS 2025 MECR mouse model (PMID 41021813). Now hunting the MECR/AJHG-2021 brothers paper via a MECR-wide search.", "reasoning_content": "So the three PMIDs:\n- 34211152 = Manickam et al., Genet Med 2021 — ACMG guideline \"Exome and genome sequencing for pediatric patients with congenital anomalies or intellectual disability\" (DEP 2021-07-01). This is the evidence-based guideline recommending ES/GS as first/second-tier for CA/DD/ID. Useful for §5.3 evidence grading and §3 (why WGS after ES failed).\n- 36262091 = Gupta PR, Gospe SM III (+ likely Murdock DG, Wallace DC?) — \"Ophthalmic manifestations of MEPAN syndrome\", Ophthalmic Genet 2022;43(6):469-474, doi 10.1080/13816810.2022.2135112. Confirms MEPAN phenotype: early-childhood dystonia, basal ganglia signal abnormalities on MRI, subsequent optic atrophy, relative cognitive sparing. Key phenotype source!\n- 41021813 = PNAS 2025 mouse model (e2506761122, doi 10.1073/pnas.2506761122) — Murdock DG et al. Mechanism: mtFASII loss → complex I loss, ISC assembly defects, lipoylation defects. Useful for pathogenesis + future therapy section.\n\nWait — which PMID is Miller's Am J Hum Genet 2021 diagnostic odyssey paper? Not in these three. The Miller 2021 AJHG paper is \"Ten Years of the Undiagnosed Diseases Network...\" or specifically the one with the brothers? Let me think: The AJHG 2021 paper describing two brothers with MEPAN found via UDN Stanford — that could be Heeley/Shinawi? No. There's a known AJHG 2021 paper: \"Mitochondrial enoyl-CoA reductase protein-associated neurodegeneration\" — the original MEPAN description was Heimer et al. 2016 AJHG (\"A recessive MECR mutation...\"? Actually Heimer G et al., AJHG 2016, \"MECR-related neurodegeneration\"). The 2021 Miller paper: \"Miller D, ... Am J Hum Genet 2021\" — likely \"The Undiagnosed Diseases Network: Accelerating...\"? Hmm, there IS an AJHG 2021 perspective by the UDN: \"Ten Years of the Undiagnosed Diseases Network\" — no, that's 2024? There's also \"Miller et al. 2021 AJHG — 'A single-center UDN...'\"? \n\nActually I recall: Fuki Hisama + Timothy Yu + Danny Miller — \"Genetic diagnosis of a rare neurologic disease...\"? The trio (Miller D, Yu TW, Hisama FM) co-authored the ACMG guideline paper (34211152). The MEPAN brothers case report might be: \"Miller DE? ... 'MECR-associated neurodegeneration: expanding...'\"? \n\nLet me just search PubMed for it: term=MECR+AND+Undiagnosed or term=\"mitochondrial enoyl\" AND brothers. Or search Am J Hum Genet[ta] AND MECR. Let me do that. Also search for the original Heimer 2016 paper (PMID ~27569546?) for the founding phenotype.\n\nAlso fetch: term=MECR[tiab] to get the full MECR literature list (Heimer 2016, the 2021 AJHG case, maybe a 2023 review). Let me run that crawl now. Also update consult_file.md §1 and start §2 with what's verified so far.\n\nActually, to be efficient: one crawl for term=MECR[tiab]&format=pubmed, then mine. And in parallel, update the file with §1 + §2 draft. Let me do the crawl first (single call), then file update while mining.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-ab02a3932244c484", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "web_crawl", "arguments": "{\"max_pages\": 2, \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=MECR%5Btiab%5D&format=pubmed\"}"}}], "step": 26, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 949, "prompt_tokens": 24580, "total_tokens": 25529, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 811}}}
