++{"seq": 151, "ts": 1792081842.749, "role": "assistant", "content": "All seven sources are now verified with full abstracts. Writing the complete consult file.", "reasoning_content": "Confirmed: PMID 37734847 = Heimer et al., Am J Hum Genet 2016 Dec 1;99(6):1229-1244, doi 10.1016/j.ajhg.2016.09.021, \"MECR Mutations Cause Childhood-Onset Dystonia and Optic Atrophy, a Mitochondrial Fatty Acid Synthesis Disorder.\" Journal: Am J Hum Genet (IS 0002-9297). Full abstract captured. All key facts verified:\n\n- 7 individuals, 5 families, childhood-onset dystonia, optic atrophy, basal ganglia signal abnormalities on MRI\n- recessive MECR mutations, 6 mutations listed\n- fibroblasts: reduced MECR, reduced lipoylated proteins, defective respiration\n- decreased lipoylation → potential therapeutic strategy\n\nI now have all 7 sources verified. Time to write the consult file. ~35 min elapsed. Writing the full consult now with all sections. I'll write it in one comprehensive write_file (the file already exists with skeleton; I'll replace it entirely with the complete version).\n\nKey content plan:\n\n**§1 Case summary** [REF] with explicit NOT IN MY CONTEXT items (birth history, consanguinity, head growth, seizures, current ages, cognitive status, exact MRI findings beyond \"basal ganglia T2 abnormalities\", visual status, lab values).\n\n**§2 Leading diagnosis (committed):** MEPAN syndrome (mitochondrial enoyl-CoA reductase protein-associated neurodegeneration) = MECR-related neurologic disorder. Rationale: (a) two affected male sibs → autosomal recessive consistent [REF; GeneReviews S5 AR]; (b) early motor delay + hypotonia then stiff jerky movements = evolving childhood-onset movement disorder (dystonia/chorea/atacia) — GeneReviews: presents 1–6.5y, mainly dystonia ± chorea/ataxia [S5]; (c) diagnosed CP at 16 months but with later REGRESSION — CP is by definition non-progressive; regression + basal ganglia T2 abnormalities points to genetic/metabolic neurodegeneration [REF +