h XML -->   <link rel="search" type="application/opensearchdescription+xml" href="https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/persistent/opensearch.xml" title="PubMed search">    <!-- Disables severely broken elements when no JS -->   <noscript>     <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/a447896c-976f-490b-b86b-2668b65114a8/core/no-script.css">   </noscript>         <link rel="canonical" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=MEPAN%5Btiab%5D+AND+2021%5Bdp%5D&amp;format=pubmed" />      </head> <body >       <main class="search-page" id="search-page">     <div class="search-results" id="search-results">                <pre class="search-results-chunk">PMID- 32644907\r OWN - NLM\r STAT- MEDLINE\r DCOM- 20211108\r LR  - 20211108\r IS  - 1089-4098 (Electronic)\r IS  - 1073-8584 (Linking)\r VI  - 27\r IP  - 2\r DP  - 2021 Apr\r TI  - Mitochondrial Fatty Acids and Neurodegenerative Disorders.\r PG  - 143-158\r LID - 10.1177/1073858420936162 [doi]\r AB  - Fatty acids in mitochondria, in sensu stricto, arise either as β-oxidation \r       substrates imported via the carnitine shuttle or through de novo synthesis by the \r       mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis (mtFAS) pathway. Defects in mtFAS or processes \r       involved in the generation of the mtFAS product derivative lipoic acid (LA), \r       including iron-sulfur cluster synthesis required for functional LA synthase, have \r       emerged only recently as etiology for neurodegenerative disease. Intriguingly, \r       mtFAS deficiencies very specifically affect CNS function, while LA synthesis and \r       attachment defects have a pleiotropic presentation beyond neurodegeneration. \r       Typical mtFAS defect presentations include optical atrophy, as well as basal \r       ganglia defects associated with dystonia. The phenotype display of patients with \r       mtFAS defects can resemble the presentation of disorders associated with coenzyme \r       A (CoA) synthesis. A recent publication links these processes together based on \r       the requirement of CoA for acyl carrier protein maturation. MtFAS defects, CoA \r       synthesis- as well as Fe-S cluster-deficiencies share lack of LA as a common \r       symptom.\r FAU - Kastaniotis, Alexander J\r AU  - Kastaniotis AJ\r AUID- ORCID: 0000-0003-3624-9214\r AD  - Faculty of Biochemistry and Molecular Medicine, University of Oulu, Oulu, \r       Finland.\r FAU - Autio, Kaija J\r AU  - Autio KJ\r AD  - Faculty of Biochemistry and Molecular Medicine, University of Oulu, Oulu, \r       Finland.\r FAU - R Nair, Remya\r AU  - R Nair R\r AUID- ORCID: 0000-0001-9007-5740\r AD  - Mammalian Genetics Unit, MRC Harwell Institute, Oxfordshire, UK.\r LA  - eng\r PT  - Journal Article\r PT  - Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov&#x27;t\r PT  - Review\r DEP - 20200709\r PL  - United States\r TA  - Neuroscientist\r JT  - The Neuroscientist : a review journal bringing neurobiology, neurology and \r       psychiatry\r JID - 9504819\r RN  - 0 (Fatty Acids)\r RN  - SAA04E81UX (Coenzyme A)\r SB  - IM\r MH  - Animals\r MH  - Coenzyme A/biosynthesis/genetics\r MH  - Fatty Acids/*biosynthesis/genetics\r MH  - Humans\r MH  - Mitochondria/genetics/*metabolism\r MH  - Neurodegenerative Diseases/genetics/*metabolism\r MH  - Signal Transduction/*physiology\r OTO - NOTNLM\r OT  - CoA synthesis\r OT  - CoPAN\r OT  - MEPAN\r OT  - PKAN\r OT  - acyl carrier protein\r OT  - iron-sulfur cluster synthesis\r OT  - lipoic acid\r OT  - mitochondrial fatty acid synthesis\r OT  - neurodegeneration\r EDAT- 2020/07/10 06:00\r MHDA- 2021/11/09 06:00\r CRDT- 2020/07/10 06:00\r PHST- 2020/07/10 06:00 [pubmed]\r PHST- 2021/11/09 06:00 [medline]\r PHST- 2020/07/10 06:00 [entrez]\r AID - 10.1177/1073858420936162 [doi]\r PST - ppublish\r SO  - Neuroscientist. 2021 Apr;27(2):143-158. doi: 10.1177/1073858420936162. Epub 2020 \r       Jul 9.\r \r PMID- 33545028\r OWN - NLM\r STAT- MEDLINE\r DCOM- 20210219\r LR  - 20210806\r IS  - 1537-6605 (Electronic)\r IS  - 0002-9297 (Print)\r IS  - 0002-9297 (Linking)\r VI  - 108\r IP  - 2\r DP  - 2021 Feb 4\r TI  - The diagnostic odyssey: our family&#x27;s story.\r PG  - 217-218\r LID - S0002-9297(21)00003-3 [pii]\r LID - 10.1016/j.ajhg.2021.01.003 [doi]\r AB  - Danny is the father of two boys with MEPAN syndrome and a member of Global Genes&#x27; \r       RARE Foundation Alliance Leadership Council.\r CI  - Copyright © 2021.\r FAU - Miller, Danny\r AU  - Miller D\r AD  - Corte Madera, CA, USA. Electronic address: danny@mepan.org.\r LA  - eng\r PT  - Journal Article\r PT  - Personal Narrative\r PL  - United States\r TA  - Am J Hum Genet\r JT  - American journal of human genetics\r JID - 0370475\r RN  - EC 1.3.- (Oxidoreductases Acting on CH-CH Group Donors)\r RN  - EC 1.3.1.38 (trans-2-enoyl-CoA reductase (NADPH))\r SB  - IM\r CIN - Am J Hum Genet. 2021 Feb 4;108(2):213. doi: 10.1016/j.ajhg.2021.01.005. PMID: \r       33545026\r MH  - Genetic Diseases, Inborn/*diagnosis/genetics\r MH  - Genetic Research\r MH  - Genetic Testing\r MH  - Heredodegenerative Disorders, Nervous System/*diagnosis/genetics\r MH  - Humans\r MH  - Information Dissemination\r MH  - Male\r MH  - Oxidoreductases Acting on CH-CH Group Donors/*genetics\r MH  - Rare Diseases/*diagnosis/genetics\r MH  - Syndrome\r MH  - Whole Genome Sequencing\r PMC - PMC8175868\r COIS- The author declares no competing interests.\r EDAT- 2021/02/06 06:00\r MHDA- 2021/02/20 06:00\r PMCR- 2021/08/04\r CRDT- 2021/02/05 20:08\r PHST- 2021/02/05 20:08 [entrez]\r PHST- 2021/02/06 06:00 [pubmed]\r PHST- 2021/02/20 06:00 [medline]\r PHST- 2021/08/04 00:00 [pmc-release]\r AID - S0002-9297(21)00003-3 [pii]\r AID - 10.1016/j.ajhg.2021.01.003 [doi]\r PST - ppublish\r SO  - Am J Hum Genet. 2021 Feb 4;108(2):217-218. doi: 10.1016/j.ajhg.2021.01.003.\r </pre>            </div>   </main>               </body> </html>"
